  "verdict": "orthogonal allocation preserved the first unit exactly in 12 of 12 pairs (worst error 3.052e-05), against 0 of 12 under the shared convention, and silenced the second unit in 0 of them",
  "what_exclusive_costs": "EXCLUSIVE preserves the first unit perfectly and silences the second in every pair here, because these units carry no firing condition: a first unit that fires everywhere takes every position and leaves none. That is the correct behaviour of the allocation and the reason the build path pairs it with a `when:` predicate \u2014 the linked induction unit fires on about 70% of traffic, so a second unit would still have the rest. Exclusive allocation between two unconditional units is a veto, and nothing in the preservation number alone would tell you that.",
  "on_the_tolerance": "'exactly' means within 0.0001 in float32. The worst orthogonal error was 3.052e-05, which is arithmetic noise rather than a surviving component of the second unit; the shared convention misses by up to 6.41280508, five orders of magnitude larger."
}